@* One entry in a coverage panel's "not yet played" list: something on the shelf the record has
   nothing to say about. Wears .untried, the one dashed-amber tone RecordChip and AspectChips
   wear too, so an untried thing looks untried wherever it turns up — and always a button,
   because the way to find out about it is its own reference sheet.

   Glyph is whatever identifies the subject at pill size: a spirit's colour dot, a board's
   lettered tile, an icon. Detail is the part of the entry that is not its name — the aspects
   missing from a spirit, the levels missing from a foe, a scenario's difficulty.

   .chip-lg is the shape, shared with FilterPill: both are a chip at reading size that is the
   thing being clicked, and a coverage panel's entries sit a scroll away from the filter pills
   that narrowed the list they are missing from. *@

<button type="button" @onclick="OnClick" title="@Copy.SheetTooltip(Label)"
        class="chip chip-lg untried">
    @Glyph
    <span class="@(Detail is null ? null : "font-medium")">@Label</span>
    @if (Detail is not null)
    {
        <span class="text-amber-700">@Detail</span>
    }
</button>

@code {
    /// <summary>The subject's name — also what the tooltip names as the sheet this opens.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Label { get; set; } = "";

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public EventCallback OnClick { get; set; }

    /// <summary>What identifies the subject at pill size — a colour dot, a letter tile, an icon.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Glyph { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The rest of the entry: which aspects, which levels, what it adds to the difficulty.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Detail { get; set; }
}
